  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes\n\n- A method returning an IAsyncStateMachine type gets an imposter that compiles (#427, closes #425). Such a method was treated as async, so its imposter awaited a type that can't be awaited and failed with CS1983, CS4010 and CS8716. A method is now async only when it returns Task, ValueTask, Task<T> or ValueTask<T>, the same rule events already used.\n\nPerformance\n\n- Fewer allocations per call for async outcomes, indexer getters and async events (#419, closes #402). Fixed async returns and exceptions are created once during setup instead of on every call, a callback-only indexer getter no longer creates a bound delegate, and raising an async event with no handlers no longer allocates a task list. A fixed Task exception drops from 512 to 96 bytes per call.\n\n  A fixed ReturnsAsync or ThrowsAsync outcome now hands every call the same completed task, so code that compares tasks by reference sees one task instead of a new one per call.",
